<title>USA: Apple cuts price on messagepad.</title>
<headline>Apple cuts price on messagepad.</headline>
<dateline>CUPERTINO, Calif. 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Apple Computer Inc said it has reduced the price of its MessagePad 130 from a suggested retail price of $799 to a suggested retail price of $699.</p>
<p>It also said it is offering Win2Go Office Companion for Newton software free with its MessagePad 130 handheld computer between now and January 31, 1997.</p>
<p>Purchasers in the United States and Canada will be entitled to one free copy of Win2Go software from PICA Information and Management GmbH, having an estimated retail value of $180 to $190.</p>
